1
00:00:09,277 --> 00:00:11,927
=The Glory Fades 2=

2
00:00:11,927 --> 00:00:13,798
=Episode 4=

3
00:00:20,809 --> 00:00:22,610
Solitary confinement's over, come out.

4
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:32,850
Captain Xia.

5
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:37,210
4167,

6
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:38,490
you're staying here.

7
00:00:46,849 --> 00:00:48,250
Got it cleaned up for you already.

8
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:49,610
Top bunk or bottom bunk,

9
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:50,930
take your pick.

10
00:00:51,729 --> 00:00:53,650
No need, this is fine.

11
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:55,529
Sure thing, take a seat then.

12
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:05,370
Thanks.

13
00:01:05,409 --> 00:01:07,290
Mr. Tu, I'm Shui.

14
00:01:07,449 --> 00:01:09,370
Never thought I'd share a cell with you.

15
00:01:09,489 --> 00:01:11,010
It's an honor.

16
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:15,050
You know me?

17
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:16,610
Right after you get into the prison,

18
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:18,289
you took down Dalieba.

19
00:01:18,409 --> 00:01:19,769
Before you even reached the cell block,

20
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:21,929
you wiped the floor with Phachai's crew.

21
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:23,209
Word spread like wildfire.

22
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:24,369
Who wouldn't know you?

23
00:01:26,129 --> 00:01:27,129
Buddy,

24
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:28,569
how did you end up here?

25
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:30,289
Young and stupid,

26
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:31,690
bad temper.

27
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:33,489
Guess you've been here for long.

28
00:01:33,769 --> 00:01:36,009
Eleven years, three months,
and nine days.

29
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:37,769
Not to brag,

30
00:01:37,929 --> 00:01:40,129
in all of Sea Breeze Prison,
there's only one guy

31
00:01:40,129 --> 00:01:41,129
who's been here longer than me.

32
00:01:42,129 --> 00:01:43,649
You've seen this place.

33
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:45,330
Surviving here this long

34
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:47,090
isn't easy.

35
00:01:55,489 --> 00:01:57,890
Feng really has great taste.

36
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:00,009
Now when guests arrive,

37
00:02:00,209 --> 00:02:02,369
they see the girls right away,

38
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:04,810
no need to waste time picking.

39
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:06,610
If they like one, they just take her.

40
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:08,970
Is there any difference
from the sleaziest dive bar?

41
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:11,409
Prosperity succeeded

42
00:02:11,929 --> 00:02:13,289
because Jiasheng

43
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:15,090
built its reputation step by step.

44
00:02:16,409 --> 00:02:17,409
This brand name

45
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:20,249
isn't something you can just ruin.

46
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:23,209
Ruin it then.

47
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:26,130
Tear it down and rebuild it better.

48
00:02:26,489 --> 00:02:27,489
Manni.

49
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:31,769
What is all this junk?

50
00:02:31,809 --> 00:02:33,130
Piled up all over the VIP rooms.

51
00:02:36,369 --> 00:02:37,689
You don't know what these are?

52
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:39,769
Stop playing innocent.

53
00:02:41,089 --> 00:02:42,610
We run a nightclub.

54
00:02:42,969 --> 00:02:45,050
Making guests happy is our top priority.

55
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:47,369
Whatever the guests want,

56
00:02:47,369 --> 00:02:48,689
we give it to them.

57
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:50,170
Jiasheng made a rule.

58
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:51,809
We don't do things like this.

59
00:02:52,249 --> 00:02:53,249
Jiasheng?

60
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:56,570
You mean the murderer?

61
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:58,730
He's rotting in Sea Breeze Prison.

62
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:00,689
Let's see if he can make it out alive.

63
00:03:07,489 --> 00:03:08,489
Hey, buddy,

64
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:10,809
can I ask you something?

65
00:03:14,089 --> 00:03:15,209
I can't take this.

66
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:16,610
Just ask whatever you want.

67
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:20,929
Take it.

68
00:03:25,969 --> 00:03:27,769
All right, go ahead.

69
00:03:27,769 --> 00:03:29,089
I'll tell you everything I know.

70
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:30,689
Tell me about Sea Breeze.

71
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:33,330
It has two big bosses

72
00:03:33,529 --> 00:03:34,929
you don't want to mess with.

73
00:03:35,890 --> 00:03:37,170
Cross them, and you're done for.

74
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:38,890
And funny enough,

75
00:03:39,209 --> 00:03:41,170
you've already crossed both of them.

76
00:03:41,809 --> 00:03:42,929
The first one

77
00:03:43,809 --> 00:03:44,809
is Lion.

78
00:03:45,689 --> 00:03:46,809
(In Sea Breeze,)

79
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:49,369
(Boss Lion is the top guy
you never cross.)

80
00:03:49,529 --> 00:03:51,620
(He was a mercenary,)

81
00:03:52,314 --> 00:03:53,843
(seen real combat, real blood,)

82
00:03:54,783 --> 00:03:56,542
(crawled out of a pile of corpses.)

83
00:03:56,696 --> 00:03:59,335
(When it comes to brawling,
no one here can touch him.)

84
00:03:59,696 --> 00:04:01,055
(He's fiercely loyal,)

85
00:04:01,216 --> 00:04:03,136
(takes great care of his boys.)

86
00:04:03,256 --> 00:04:05,416
(Lay a finger on one of them,)

87
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:06,657
(and he'll hunt you down.)

88
00:04:06,657 --> 00:04:07,739
Lion!

89
00:04:08,324 --> 00:04:10,665
- Lion!
- Lion!

90
00:04:10,665 --> 00:04:13,905
(- That guy you knocked out was Dalieba.)
- Lion!

91
00:04:13,905 --> 00:04:15,358
(- Lion's man.)
- Lion!

92
00:04:15,745 --> 00:04:17,345
Now that you've made an enemy of him,

93
00:04:17,426 --> 00:04:18,945
you'd better watch your back.

94
00:04:20,185 --> 00:04:21,505
The other one is Phachai,

95
00:04:21,706 --> 00:04:22,745
whom you've also met.

96
00:04:23,065 --> 00:04:25,026
(He's shrewd,
knows how to play the game,)

97
00:04:25,266 --> 00:04:27,586
(and is tight with Warden Tang Zhen.)

98
00:04:27,785 --> 00:04:30,116
(So he is in charge of all the booze
and smokes here.)

99
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:31,163
(Those two things are gold
around here.)

100
00:04:31,163 --> 00:04:32,465
How did it become three hundred?

101
00:04:32,946 --> 00:04:33,946
You want it or not?

102
00:04:36,746 --> 00:04:37,746
Give me a pack.

103
00:04:48,146 --> 00:04:49,146
Here.

104
00:04:54,146 --> 00:04:55,146
Ten?

105
00:04:56,305 --> 00:04:57,305
Half a pack?

106
00:04:57,465 --> 00:04:59,785
Phachai, why don't you just rob me?

107
00:05:04,225 --> 00:05:05,425
I am robbing you.

108
00:05:05,746 --> 00:05:06,746
What's the problem?

109
00:05:10,865 --> 00:05:11,865
No booze, then?

110
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:14,386
You scammed me out of every penny.

111
00:05:14,386 --> 00:05:15,586
I can't buy squat!

112
00:05:18,066 --> 00:05:19,066
What about Captain Xia?

113
00:05:19,225 --> 00:05:20,225
What's

114
00:05:20,305 --> 00:05:21,305
her deal?

115
00:05:21,305 --> 00:05:22,305
Captain Xia?

116
00:05:22,826 --> 00:05:24,105
Don't let her looks fool you.

117
00:05:24,545 --> 00:05:26,026
She's ruthless.

118
00:05:26,266 --> 00:05:29,105
This is Officer Xia Yuyan.

119
00:05:29,305 --> 00:05:30,905
She'll be in charge of maximum security.

120
00:05:31,465 --> 00:05:33,225
(She's not just
the captain of the guards,)

121
00:05:33,425 --> 00:05:36,266
(but also a special envoy
from Central Inspection Ministry.)

122
00:05:36,506 --> 00:05:38,826
(Even Warden Tang Zhen
treads lightly around her.)

123
00:05:45,626 --> 00:05:46,905
Well, look at that.

124
00:05:46,905 --> 00:05:49,465
A female guard in Sea Breeze.

125
00:05:54,706 --> 00:05:55,706
Sweetheart,

126
00:05:55,865 --> 00:05:57,105
you don't belong here.

127
00:05:57,305 --> 00:05:59,186
Don't worry,

128
00:05:59,225 --> 00:06:00,345
I'll take good care of you.

129
00:06:02,105 --> 00:06:03,105
Darn, so tough!

130
00:06:03,781 --> 00:06:04,781
Darn, so tough!

131
00:06:08,706 --> 00:06:10,225
Watch your filthy mouth.

132
00:06:10,665 --> 00:06:11,665
Do that again,

133
00:06:12,146 --> 00:06:14,186
and I'll make sure you disappear.

134
00:06:16,066 --> 00:06:17,225
(Still,)

135
00:06:17,425 --> 00:06:18,425
(she's fair.)

136
00:06:18,746 --> 00:06:20,026
Clean as a whistle.

137
00:06:20,905 --> 00:06:22,345
Never seen her take a bribe.

138
00:06:22,425 --> 00:06:23,626
And she doesn't push people around.

139
00:06:25,985 --> 00:06:28,826
Now this looks like a proper business.

140
00:06:30,706 --> 00:06:32,186
This isn't Prosperity anymore.

141
00:06:32,386 --> 00:06:33,425
Jiasheng used to say...

142
00:06:33,425 --> 00:06:35,026
Feng is talking now.

143
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,105
Ruxue,

144
00:06:38,425 --> 00:06:39,425
great job.

145
00:06:39,706 --> 00:06:40,826
I like it.

146
00:06:41,186 --> 00:06:42,626
As long as you're pleased, Feng.

147
00:06:43,105 --> 00:06:46,105
Manni, Jiasheng can't help you
from inside,

148
00:06:46,586 --> 00:06:47,985
much less help the club.

149
00:06:48,586 --> 00:06:51,305
From now on, you'd better listen to me.

150
00:06:52,865 --> 00:06:53,865
Manni,

151
00:06:54,465 --> 00:06:56,386
that Mr. Zhang is a sicko!

152
00:06:56,465 --> 00:06:57,545
He hit me!

153
00:06:57,545 --> 00:06:58,826
He burned me with cigarettes!

154
00:06:58,826 --> 00:06:59,826
I quit!

155
00:06:59,826 --> 00:07:00,905
I can't do this anymore!

156
00:07:00,905 --> 00:07:01,905
It's okay.

157
00:07:01,946 --> 00:07:03,626
I'm here, don't be afraid. I've got you.

158
00:07:06,865 --> 00:07:07,865
What are you doing?

159
00:07:07,985 --> 00:07:09,266
I'll show you what I'm doing.

160
00:07:09,266 --> 00:07:10,826
Let me see what you can do.

161
00:07:11,186 --> 00:07:12,186
Lu.

162
00:07:15,865 --> 00:07:16,946
Let me introduce you.

163
00:07:17,785 --> 00:07:18,905
This is Du Qiang,

164
00:07:19,465 --> 00:07:21,266
just got back from abroad.

165
00:07:21,586 --> 00:07:23,665
From now on, the security here

166
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:25,266
is under his full control.

167
00:07:25,506 --> 00:07:26,506
Say hello to Lu.

168
00:07:29,105 --> 00:07:30,105
Hello.

169
00:07:32,225 --> 00:07:34,105
Get back in there and serve the guest.

170
00:07:34,266 --> 00:07:35,266
She's hurt.

171
00:07:35,665 --> 00:07:36,785
I'm taking her to get patched up.

172
00:07:41,985 --> 00:07:42,985
Fine.

173
00:07:43,225 --> 00:07:44,225
Down to business.

174
00:07:45,746 --> 00:07:46,746
Lu,

175
00:07:47,946 --> 00:07:49,066
I've decided

176
00:07:49,706 --> 00:07:50,905
to run for Council Speaker.

177
00:07:51,225 --> 00:07:52,905
Prosperity

178
00:07:53,105 --> 00:07:55,706
will be my primary base
for winning votes.

179
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:58,305
Lots of high-profile figures

180
00:07:58,545 --> 00:07:59,706
will be meeting here.

181
00:08:02,425 --> 00:08:03,425
You need to

182
00:08:03,425 --> 00:08:04,746
expand the scale

183
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:06,545
and step up service quality.

184
00:08:06,706 --> 00:08:09,266
Treat every single guest like royalty.

185
00:08:09,586 --> 00:08:11,865
Understood. Congratulations, Feng.

186
00:08:13,026 --> 00:08:14,146
Oh, no.

187
00:08:14,305 --> 00:08:16,545
Congratulations, Mr. Speaker.

188
00:08:18,026 --> 00:08:19,146
Do you know this man?

189
00:08:22,386 --> 00:08:23,386
Old Ghost.

190
00:08:23,785 --> 00:08:26,066
He was already here when I arrived.

191
00:08:26,305 --> 00:08:27,425
The guy I mentioned

192
00:08:27,785 --> 00:08:29,905
who's been here longer than me,

193
00:08:30,146 --> 00:08:31,146
that's him.

194
00:08:31,826 --> 00:08:33,626
How can I meet him?

195
00:08:34,545 --> 00:08:35,746
You can't.

196
00:08:36,066 --> 00:08:37,066
He's a special case.

197
00:08:37,506 --> 00:08:38,706
Half a month in solitary,

198
00:08:38,785 --> 00:08:39,985
half a month in a villa.

199
00:08:41,185 --> 00:08:43,305
Warden Tang Zhen guards him personally.

200
00:08:43,785 --> 00:08:45,386
Regular inmates

201
00:08:45,986 --> 00:08:47,185
can't even get close.

202
00:08:49,466 --> 00:08:51,026
What a shame.

203
00:08:52,106 --> 00:08:54,825
Tang, how many times
do I have to tell you?

204
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:56,746
Throwing me in solitary is fine,

205
00:08:56,825 --> 00:08:57,825
right?

206
00:08:58,065 --> 00:09:00,146
At least have someone
water my vegetables!

207
00:09:00,226 --> 00:09:01,226
Look at them,

208
00:09:01,266 --> 00:09:02,266
completely withered.

209
00:09:02,266 --> 00:09:03,986
Hand over the goods,

210
00:09:04,665 --> 00:09:06,705
and you can live here forever,

211
00:09:06,785 --> 00:09:08,905
growing your veggies
and tending flowers in peace.

212
00:09:12,905 --> 00:09:13,905
Old Ghost,

213
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:15,466
we've dragged this out for years.

214
00:09:15,466 --> 00:09:16,746
You're getting on in years.

215
00:09:16,866 --> 00:09:17,866
It's not worth it.

216
00:09:21,425 --> 00:09:23,146
Taste this cucumber I grew.

217
00:09:23,866 --> 00:09:25,866
Not a trace of pesticide.

218
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,305
Taste it, pure and authentic.

219
00:09:28,825 --> 00:09:29,825
Go ahead, eat it.

220
00:09:30,585 --> 00:09:31,585
Fine.

221
00:09:32,785 --> 00:09:34,386
Then we'll keep waiting it out.

222
00:09:43,106 --> 00:09:44,506
There are villas in prison?

223
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:45,626
Sure are.

224
00:09:45,905 --> 00:09:46,905
Quite a few,

225
00:09:46,986 --> 00:09:48,346
luxuriously furnished,

226
00:09:48,386 --> 00:09:49,466
with everything you could want.

227
00:09:50,026 --> 00:09:51,226
Even women, if you ask.

228
00:09:53,346 --> 00:09:55,506
Get on your knees and crawl over.

229
00:10:06,545 --> 00:10:09,226
Look at me.

230
00:10:15,146 --> 00:10:17,026
To stay there,
you need serious cash first.

231
00:10:17,665 --> 00:10:19,266
A single day's stay

232
00:10:19,386 --> 00:10:21,585
costs half a year's wages
on the outside.

233
00:10:22,185 --> 00:10:23,185
And money alone won't cut it.

234
00:10:23,386 --> 00:10:25,425
Tang Zhen has to
sign off on it personally.

235
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:47,506
♪Streetlights stretch shadows long♪

236
00:10:47,876 --> 00:10:51,861
♪As crowds fade,
who lingers on the edge♪

237
00:10:56,617 --> 00:10:59,936
♪Guarding all those unfinished lies♪

238
00:10:59,936 --> 00:11:05,021
♪Wind sweeps through the empty harbor♪

239
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:15,162
♪Time quietly strips away the madness♪

240
00:11:15,162 --> 00:11:23,583
♪Plunging all passion
into freezing cold♪

241
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:26,812
♪The feast ends, leaving only emptiness♪

242
00:11:26,812 --> 00:11:30,007
♪The past drifts far away, unstoppable♪

243
00:11:30,007 --> 00:11:32,700
♪If regret is an inescapable wandering♪

244
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:37,317
♪I swallow the silence, burning alone♪

245
00:11:41,228 --> 00:11:43,717
♪Burning alone♪

246
00:11:49,223 --> 00:11:55,592
♪The glory fades♪
